Let $x_i\in\mathbb R^3$ and $p_i\in\mathbb R^3$ be the position and momentum of molecule $i$. For identical molecules of mass $m$, take $H(X,P)=
 \sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{p_i^2}{2m}
 +\sum_{i<j}u\!\left(|x_i-x_j|\right),$ where $X=(x_1,\ldots,x_N)$ and $P=(p_1,\ldots,p_N)$. The restriction $i<j$ excludes self-pairs and counts $(i,j)$ only once: $\sum_{i<j}1=\binom{N}{2}=\frac{N(N-1)}{2}.$

