en.math:
\begin{aligned}
 Z&=
 \frac{1}{N!h^{3N}}
 \int d^{3N}P\,d^{3N}X\\
 &\qquad{}\times e^{-\beta K(P)}e^{-\beta U(X)},\\
 K(P)&=\sum_i\frac{p_i^2}{2m}.
\end{aligned}

p.src:
Momentum and position separate. Multiplying and dividing the configurational integral by $V^N$ isolates the ideal-gas result: $\begin{aligned}
 Z
 &=\left[
 \frac{V^N}{N!h^{3N}}
 \int d^{3N}P\,e^{-\beta K(P)}
 \right] \notag\\
 &\quad\times\left[
 \frac{1}{V^N}
 \int d^{3N}X\,e^{-\beta U(X)}
 \right] \notag\\
 &\equiv Z_0\,C(\beta,V,N).
 \end{aligned}$ The familiar Gaussian factor is $\int d^{3N}P\,e^{-\beta K(P)}
 =\left(\frac{2\pi m}{\beta}\right)^{3N/2}.$

