p.src:
To first order in the interaction, $e^{-\beta U(X)}
 =1-\beta U(X)+O(U^2).$ Consequently, $\begin{aligned}
 C
 &=
 1-\frac{\beta}{V^N}
 \sum_{i<j}
 \int d^{3N}X\,u(|x_i-x_j|)
 +O(U^2) \notag\\
 &=
 1-\frac{\beta}{V^N}
 \frac{N(N-1)}{2}
 V^{N-2}(V U_0)+O(U^2) \notag\\
 &=
 1-\beta\frac{N(N-1)}{2V}U_0+O(U^2).
 \end{aligned}$ Each pair has the same integral, not the same instantaneous separation or potential energy. The remaining $N-2$ position integrals each contribute one factor of $V$.

